:: Himari - The Drawing [bg-sanctuary]
<h1 class="ptitle">THE SANCTUARY</h1>
<<run setup.himari.mark('drawing')>>
<<set _hmKept = $characters.himari.quests.drawing_kept ?? false>>
<<addmins 30>>
<br />
<<if _hmKept>>
	The guards at the gate searched you, which they had never done before. They were thorough about it. One of them found the folded square of paper inside your jacket and held it up to the light, and then he walked it up the gangway without a word.
<<else>>
	Something had happened in the yard before you got there. Her container stood open. Two guards were going through her blanket and the bucket and the cracks between the floorboards, the way men search when they have already found what they were sent for.
<</if>>
<br /><br />
Negan was standing by an oil drum near her container, where the night watch burned scrap to keep warm. It was burning now. He had a square of paper in his hand, and he was looking at it with his head tilted, like a man at a gallery.
<br /><br />
They had brought her out. She knelt on the deck beside the drum with a guard's hand on her shoulder. She saw what he was holding and went completely still.
<br /><br />
<<if _hmKept>>
	<<negan>>
		Found this in your jacket, handler. Funny place for it. You collecting art now?
	<</negan>>
<<else>>
	<<negan>>
		Boys found this in Dolly's box. Under a floorboard. Clever girl. Clever little girl.
	<</negan>>
<</if>>
<br />
He crouched in front of her and held the drawing up beside her face, so she could see it and he could see her see it.
<br /><br />
<<negan>>
	This? This is nothing, Dolly. There's no house. There's no sea. There's here, and then there's wherever I send you. That's the whole map.
<</negan>>
<br />
He held it over the drum. The edge caught. The sea went first.
<br /><br />
<center>
	<<image 'people/himari/drawing_burn.jpg'>>
</center>
<br />
She did not make a sound. She did not look away either. She watched the house go, and the tree, and the three figures in front of it, until there was nothing in his fingers but a black curl of ash, and he let it fall.
<br /><br />
<<if _hmKept>>
	<<negan>>
		Don't do that again, kid. You're the handler. You hold the chain. You don't hold her stuff.
	<</negan>>
	<br />
	He patted your cheek, twice, not hard, and walked away.
<<else>>
	He dusted off his fingers and walked away whistling. He never once looked at you.
<</if>>
<br /><br />
When the guard let go of her shoulder, she stayed kneeling by the drum and kept looking into the fire, as if something might still be in there.
<br /><br />
<<link 'Leave'>>
	<<goto 'Sanctuary'>>
<</link>>
